<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zaire</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1971–1997</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zaire was the official name of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-republic-of-the-congo">Democratic Republic of the Congo</a> from 1971 to 1997, adopted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mobutu-sese-seko">Mobutu Sese Seko</a> as part of his campaign of 'authenticity'. Under Mobutu's one-party rule the country, rich in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>, cobalt and diamonds, suffered from corruption and economic decline. In 1996–1997 an invasion by rebels under Laurent-Désiré Kabila, backed by Rwanda and Uganda, overthrew Mobutu, and the country resumed the name Democratic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republic-of-the-congo">Republic of the Congo</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zaire.jpg" alt="Zaire" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Moyogo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Zaire_(1971%E2%80%931997).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
